WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Translator: Elena Montrasio
Reviewer: Bruno Giussani

00:00:12.398 --> 00:00:14.731
[His Holiness Pope Francis
Filmed in Vatican City

00:00:14.755 --> 00:00:17.436
First shown at TED Countdown
Global Launch, October 2020]

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.610
Hello!

00:00:21.015 --> 00:00:22.889
We are living during a historic moment,

00:00:22.913 --> 00:00:26.466
marked by difficult challenges,
as we all know.

00:00:27.165 --> 00:00:29.673
The world is shaken by the crisis

00:00:29.697 --> 00:00:33.451
caused by the COVID-19 pandemic,

00:00:33.475 --> 00:00:34.760
which highlights

00:00:34.784 --> 00:00:39.012
another global challenge:

00:00:39.036 --> 00:00:42.265
the socio-environmental crisis.

00:00:43.804 --> 00:00:49.304
And this requires us, all of us,
to face a choice.

00:00:50.328 --> 00:00:53.963
The choice between what matters,

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.517
and what doesn’t.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:01.018
The choice between continuing to ignore

00:01:01.042 --> 00:01:04.242
the suffering of the poorest

00:01:04.266 --> 00:01:07.452
and to abuse our common home,

00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:09.130
our planet,

00:01:09.154 --> 00:01:12.451
or engaging at every level

00:01:12.475 --> 00:01:16.512
to transform the way we act.

00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:23.759
Science tells us, every day,
with more precision,

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.791
that urgent action is needed --

00:01:26.815 --> 00:01:30.216
and I am not dramatizing,
this is what science says --

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.349
if we are to keep the hope of avoiding

00:01:34.373 --> 00:01:37.849
radical and catastrophic climate change.

00:01:37.873 --> 00:01:40.319
And for this we must act now.

00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:43.418
This is a scientific fact.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:51.161
Our conscience tells us
that we cannot remain indifferent

00:01:51.185 --> 00:01:54.926
to the suffering of those in need,

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:59.616
to the growing economic inequalities

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.377
and social injustices.

00:02:03.108 --> 00:02:09.155
And that the economy itself cannot
be limited to production and distribution.

00:02:09.702 --> 00:02:12.546
It must also consider

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:19.111
its impacts on both the environment
and on the dignity of people.

00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:26.094
We could say that the economy

00:02:26.118 --> 00:02:29.711
should be creative

00:02:29.735 --> 00:02:33.843
in itself and in its methods,

00:02:33.867 --> 00:02:35.836
in the way it acts.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.213
Creativity.

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:41.695
I would like to invite you
to go on a journey together.

00:02:42.352 --> 00:02:46.072
A journey of transformation and of action.

00:02:46.096 --> 00:02:48.794
Made not so much of words,

00:02:48.818 --> 00:02:53.886
but rather of concrete
and pressing actions.

00:02:55.282 --> 00:03:00.117
I am calling it a journey because
it requires a shift, a change.

00:03:00.735 --> 00:03:07.353
From this crisis none of us
must come out the same --

00:03:07.377 --> 00:03:09.262
we cannot come out the same:

00:03:09.286 --> 00:03:13.594
from a crisis, we never
come out the same --

00:03:13.618 --> 00:03:18.268
and it will take time,
and hard work, to overcome it.

00:03:18.704 --> 00:03:21.796
We will have to take it
one step at a time;

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:25.370
help the weak; persuade those in doubt;

00:03:25.394 --> 00:03:28.046
imagine new solutions;

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:30.902
and commit to carry them out.

00:03:31.952 --> 00:03:33.866
Our goal is clear:

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:38.299
to build, within the next decade,

00:03:38.323 --> 00:03:43.684
a world where we can meet the needs

00:03:43.708 --> 00:03:47.169
of the present generations,

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.556
including everyone,

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:55.597
without compromising the possibilities
of future generations.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.422
I would like to invite
all people of faith,

00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:02.728
Christian or not,

00:04:02.752 --> 00:04:06.036
and all people of good will,

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:09.408
to embark on this journey,

00:04:11.448 --> 00:04:13.743
starting from your own faith,

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.432
or if you do not have a faith,
from your own intention,

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.751
from your own goodwill.

00:04:19.394 --> 00:04:23.926
Each one of us, as individuals,
or members of a group --

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:28.676
families, communities of faith,
businesses, associations, institutions --

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.820
can make a substantial contribution.

00:04:34.812 --> 00:04:39.835
Five years ago I wrote
the encyclical letter "Laudato Si’,"

00:04:39.859 --> 00:04:42.937
dedicated to the care of our common home.

00:04:43.811 --> 00:04:48.143
It proposes the concept
of "integral ecology,"

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:51.221
to respond together
to the cry of the Earth,

00:04:51.245 --> 00:04:53.959
as well as to the cry of the poor.

00:04:54.885 --> 00:04:58.051
Integral ecology is an invitation

00:04:58.075 --> 00:05:01.536
to an integral vision on life,

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:07.343
starting from the conviction
that everything in the world is connected

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:11.046
and that, as the pandemic
made sure to remind us,

00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:16.054
we are interdependent on each other,

00:05:16.078 --> 00:05:19.773
as well as on our Mother Earth.

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:24.166
From such a vision stems the need

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:27.295
to find new ways

00:05:27.319 --> 00:05:31.020
of defining progress and measuring it,

00:05:31.044 --> 00:05:35.146
without limiting ourselves
to the economic,

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:40.981
technological, financial
and gross-product aspects,

00:05:41.005 --> 00:05:44.029
but rather, giving central relevance

00:05:44.053 --> 00:05:47.435
to its ethical, social

00:05:47.459 --> 00:05:49.062
and educational dimensions.

00:05:50.454 --> 00:05:53.689
I would like to propose today
three courses of action.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:00.703
As I wrote in "Laudato Si’,"

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:06.931
the change and the right orientation
for our journey of integral ecology

00:06:06.955 --> 00:06:12.645
require first that we all take
an educational step.

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.571
So, my first suggestion

00:06:16.595 --> 00:06:20.026
is to promote, at every level,

00:06:20.050 --> 00:06:23.909
an education geared towards
the care of our common home,

00:06:23.933 --> 00:06:27.262
developing the understanding

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:33.271
that environmental problems
are linked to human needs.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.902
We must understand this
from the beginning:

00:06:37.926 --> 00:06:43.131
environmental problems
are tied to human needs.

00:06:43.647 --> 00:06:47.726
An education based on scientific data

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.322
and on an ethical approach.

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.583
This is important: both of them.

00:06:53.917 --> 00:06:57.855
I am encouraged by the fact
that many young people

00:06:57.879 --> 00:07:02.776
already show a new ecological
and social awareness,

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:06.841
and many of them fight generously

00:07:06.865 --> 00:07:09.037
for the defense of the environment

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.640
and for justice.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:16.656
As a second proposal, we must focus

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:19.479
on water and nutrition.

00:07:21.011 --> 00:07:24.602
Access to safe and drinkable water

00:07:24.626 --> 00:07:28.562
is an essential and universal human right.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:32.139
It is essential

00:07:32.163 --> 00:07:36.716
because it determines
the survival of people

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.546
and therefore is a condition

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:42.660
for the exercise of all other
rights and responsibilities.

00:07:43.516 --> 00:07:47.406
Providing adequate nutrition for all,

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:51.874
through non-destructive farming methods,

00:07:51.898 --> 00:07:55.696
should become the main purpose

00:07:55.720 --> 00:08:00.872
of the entire cycle of food
production and distribution.

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:09.136
The third suggestion
is about energy transition:

00:08:10.075 --> 00:08:14.532
a gradual replacement, but without delay,

00:08:14.556 --> 00:08:19.297
of fossil fuels with clean energy sources.

00:08:20.027 --> 00:08:22.645
We only have a few years.

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:28.060
Scientists estimate approximately

00:08:28.084 --> 00:08:30.567
less than 30 --

00:08:30.591 --> 00:08:35.016
we have a few years, less than 30 --

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.633
to drastically reduce

00:08:37.657 --> 00:08:41.838
greenhouse gas emissions
into the atmosphere.

00:08:42.484 --> 00:08:46.704
Not only must this transition be quick

00:08:46.728 --> 00:08:51.243
and capable of meeting
present and future energy needs,

00:08:51.267 --> 00:08:55.029
it also must be attentive

00:08:55.053 --> 00:08:57.900
to the impact on the poor,

00:08:57.924 --> 00:09:00.304
on local populations,

00:09:00.328 --> 00:09:04.644
as well as on those who work
in the energy production sectors.

00:09:05.433 --> 00:09:08.309
One way to encourage this change

00:09:08.333 --> 00:09:12.576
is to lead businesses
towards the urgent need

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:18.277
to commit themselves to the integral care
of our common home,

00:09:18.301 --> 00:09:20.957
excluding from investments

00:09:20.981 --> 00:09:26.878
those companies that do not meet
the parameters of integral ecology,

00:09:26.902 --> 00:09:31.404
while rewarding those
that work concretely,

00:09:31.428 --> 00:09:33.940
during this transitional phase,

00:09:33.964 --> 00:09:37.102
to put, at the center of their activities,

00:09:37.126 --> 00:09:41.053
sustainability,

00:09:41.077 --> 00:09:43.000
social justice

00:09:43.024 --> 00:09:45.421
and the promotion of the common good.

00:09:46.302 --> 00:09:50.512
Many organizations,
Catholic and of other faiths,

00:09:50.536 --> 00:09:54.510
have already taken on the responsibility

00:09:54.534 --> 00:09:57.039
to act in this direction.

00:09:57.063 --> 00:10:00.598
In fact, the Earth must be
worked and nursed,

00:10:00.622 --> 00:10:03.443
cultivated and protected.

00:10:03.959 --> 00:10:10.286
We cannot continue
to squeeze it like an orange.

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:16.595
And we can say that this --
taking care of the Earth --

00:10:16.619 --> 00:10:18.348
is a human right.

00:10:21.071 --> 00:10:24.232
These three proposals
must be considered

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:27.688
as part of a larger group of actions

00:10:27.712 --> 00:10:31.419
that we must carry out
in an integrated way

00:10:31.443 --> 00:10:35.486
in order to find a lasting solution
to these problems.

00:10:37.255 --> 00:10:41.256
The current economic system
is unsustainable.

00:10:41.905 --> 00:10:47.187
We are faced with the moral imperative,
and the practical urgency,

00:10:47.211 --> 00:10:50.308
to rethink many things:

00:10:50.332 --> 00:10:54.676
the way we produce; the way we consume;

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.916
our culture of waste;

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:00.396
our short-term vision;

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.601
the exploitation of the poor

00:11:02.625 --> 00:11:06.056
and our indifference towards them;

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:08.877
the growing inequalities

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:12.918
and our dependence
on harmful energy sources.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.584
We need to think about
all these challenges.

00:11:18.654 --> 00:11:23.724
Integral ecology suggests a new conception

00:11:23.748 --> 00:11:27.141
of the relationship between
us humans and Nature.

00:11:28.225 --> 00:11:30.705
This leads to a new economy,

00:11:30.729 --> 00:11:33.569
where the production of wealth

00:11:33.593 --> 00:11:38.292
is directed to the integral well-being
of the human being

00:11:38.316 --> 00:11:40.062
and to the improvement --

00:11:40.086 --> 00:11:42.121
not the destruction --

00:11:42.145 --> 00:11:44.281
of our common home.

00:11:44.976 --> 00:11:48.778
It also implies a renewed politics,

00:11:48.802 --> 00:11:53.807
conceived as one
of the highest forms of charity.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:56.903
Yes,

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:02.523
love is interpersonal,

00:12:02.547 --> 00:12:04.756
but love is also political.

00:12:06.883 --> 00:12:10.320
It involves all peoples
and it involves Nature.

00:12:12.037 --> 00:12:15.967
I invite therefore all of you

00:12:15.991 --> 00:12:18.714
to embark on this journey,

00:12:18.738 --> 00:12:21.689
that I proposed in "Laudato Si’"

00:12:21.713 --> 00:12:25.937
and also in my new encyclical
"Fratelli Tutti."

00:12:26.815 --> 00:12:30.980
As the term Countdown suggests,

00:12:31.004 --> 00:12:33.470
we must act with urgency.

00:12:34.284 --> 00:12:39.119
Each one of us can play a valuable role,

00:12:39.143 --> 00:12:43.175
if we all begin our journey today --

00:12:43.199 --> 00:12:45.215
not tomorrow -- today.

00:12:45.614 --> 00:12:50.377
Because the future is built today,

00:12:50.401 --> 00:12:55.044
and it is not built in isolation,

00:12:55.068 --> 00:12:58.542
but rather in community and in harmony.

00:12:59.529 --> 00:13:01.054
Thank you.

